      "content": "I'm currently looking at a collection of diagnostic sherds from a late Bronze Age stratum. I'm having some trouble distinguishing between different firing environments based solely on the surface oxidation. Does the presence of localized dark spotting or \"mottling\" usually indicate an uneven kiln atmosphere, or could it be a result of specific temper inclusions during the paste preparation?",
